{
  "id": "rustvalley",
  "name": "Rust Valley",
  "_comment": [
    "A node is a place, not a map. Its plan is the three acts of taking it:",
    "  breakthrough - break the defensive line (symmetric 5CP, both sides push)",
    "  assault      - take the positions behind it (attack/defend, BLU attacks)",
    "  advance      - bring the bomb in and blow the objective (payload)",
    "A stage names no map. It names a kind, and battlefields[kind] is where",
    "that kind can be fought and how many people each of those takes. The",
    "coordinator picks from the pool using the map votes of whoever is queued",
    "and how many of them there are, so a node plays differently every time it",
    "is fought over without anybody writing a second theater file.",
    "skirmish is the small-population stage: arena and koth, two to twelve a",
    "side. Give a node a skirmish first if you want it winnable at 2v2."
  ],
